From: zhangjianguo <janegle@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: validate WCID index before WTBL lookup

The mt7996 driver does not validate WCID indices from TX free events
and TX status reports before WTBL lookups. An out-of-range WCID causes
invalid MMIO accesses. On the Airoha NPU RX path this is observed as a
WARNING in mt7996_mac_wtbl_lmac_addr via mt7996_mac_add_txs and can
degrade Wi-Fi traffic.

Add bounds checks against mt7996_wtbl_size() in mt7996_mac_tx_free()
and mt7996_mac_add_txs(), matching the fix posted upstream by Joshua
Klinesmith.

Signed-off-by: zhangjianguo <janegle@gmail.com>
---
 mt7996/mac.c | 6 ++++++

diff --git a/mt7996/mac.c b/mt7996/mac.c
--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -1397,6 +1397,9 @@
 			u16 idx;
 
 			idx = FIELD_GET(MT_TXFREE_INFO_WLAN_ID, info);
+			if (idx >= mt7996_wtbl_size(dev))
+				goto next;
+
 			wcid = mt76_wcid_ptr(dev, idx);
 			sta = wcid_to_sta(wcid);
 			if (!sta) {
@@ -1634,6 +1637,9 @@
 	u8 pid;
 
 	wcidx = le32_get_bits(txs_data[2], MT_TXS2_WCID);
+	if (wcidx >= mt7996_wtbl_size(dev))
+		return;
+
 	pid = le32_get_bits(txs_data[3], MT_TXS3_PID);
 
 	if (pid < MT_PACKET_ID_NO_SKB)

-- 
2.51.0
